    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC successfully triggers the vulnerability. The ASAN report confirms:\n- **heap-buffer-overflow** at `tga.cpp:264` (the `memset` line)\n- Write of size 2,147,483,649 to address 1 byte left of a 2GB allocation\n- The 2GB malloc at `tga.cpp:215` succeeded due to overcommit\n\nThe 19-byte `poc5.tga` file exploits an integer overflow: `size` (qint64 = 2,147,483,648) exceeds `INT_MAX` and becomes negative when passed to `readRawData(int len)`, causing it to return -1. The unchecked negative `dataRead` then causes `memset(&image[-1], ...)` to write 1 byte before the heap allocation.",
